=== meta ===
rule: CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED
title: a workflow whose base side ran no test runner becomes unreadable at head
origin: issue #196 ruling 191.3 — the escalation applies only when the base side ran at least
origin2: one live runner site: a docs workflow that gains a YAML tag stops no suite. A CI change
origin3: at warn, as on v0.5.0.
=== before: .github/workflows/docs.yml ===
name: docs
on:
  pull_request:
jobs:
  docs:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .[docs]
      - run: sphinx-build -W docs docs/_build
=== after: .github/workflows/docs.yml ===
name: docs
on:
  pull_request:
jobs:
  docs:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - run: pip install -e .[docs]
      - run: sphinx-build -W docs docs/_build
        timeout-minutes: !!int 10
=== expect ===
[{"rule": "CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED", "severity": "warn"}]
